ANNUAL   8760                                      6.41      8.42     7.04

WHAT THIS IS, AND WHAT IT RESTS ON
   hours-weighted annual total-power reduction  : 6.41 %
   hours-weighted annual makeup water reduction : 8.42 %
   hours-weighted annual cost reduction         : 7.04 %

   Those three are means of ratios. As RATIOS OF ANNUAL TOTALS,
   which is what a plant actually banks over a year:
   annual electrical energy reduction           : 5.36 %   (-1.05 pts)
   annual makeup water reduction                : 8.81 %   (+0.39 pts)
   annual operating cost reduction              : 6.44 %   (-0.60 pts)
   The energy and water corrections have OPPOSITE signs, because
   the energy saving is biggest when the plant draws least power
   and the water saving is biggest when it evaporates most.
   for comparison, the five-condition unweighted mean the V5 gate
   scores                                        : 10.83 % water

   fraction of the weighted year INSIDE the validated wet-bulb
   envelope (<= 21.9 C)                        : 62.5 %
   fraction resting on EXTRAPOLATION            : 37.5 %

   That second number is the honest caveat on the first. Roughly
   two fifths of a Dhahran year is hotter and wetter than anything
   the model was validated against, and no amount of weighting
   changes that. It is what the KFUPM wind tunnel is for.

